      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- academic year description: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\n- geometric mean of the number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- library subjects: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- subjects with more than zero enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- departments that offered such subjects: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- subjects offered per academic term: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- number of subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- range of the number of subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- variance of the number of subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- standard deviation of the number of subjects offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- variability category: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, the geometric mean of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during that year (considering only subjects with more than zero enrolled students), the number of distinct departments that offered such subjects in that year, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of subjects offered per academic term in that year (considering only terms where at least one subject was offered), and the variability category for the year (classified as 'HIGH_VARIABILITY' if the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) is at least 20% greater than the average standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) across all years, 'LOW_VARIABILITY' if at least 20% less, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise)? List the results ordered by geometric mean enrollment in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers."
