      "content": "The database connection is failing with an access-denied error, so I cannot run verification queries. I'll base the final SQL entirely on the semantic-network evidence and precedent metrics, which are comprehensive.\n\n---\n\n# Phase 2 Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables:**\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** — Extended academic term dimension covering *all* terms known to the warehouse (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS). Carries `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, `FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR`, `DEGREE_YEAR`, term dates. Lacks `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS`, `ADD_DATE`, `DROP_DATE`. Granularity: one row per academic term (all terms).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Status-tracked term dimension (subset of ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL). Same calendar/year columns plus `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS`, `ADD_DATE`, `DROP_DATE`. Granularity: one row per academic term.\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Subjects offered per term within library reserve processing scope. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject per library records\"). Granularity: one row per subject per term in library reserve scope.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Textbook Information Program subjects offered per term. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL`. Granularity: one row per subject per term in the textbook program.\n\n**Metrics (precedents retrieved with full SQL):**\n- **dw_1301** — Per-academic-year STDDEV of `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, joining `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` on TERM_CODE; groups by `ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`.\n- **dw_4701** — Per-academic-year geometric mean via `EXP(AVG(LN(x)))`, grouped by ACADEMIC_YEAR + ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, ordered by the geometric mean DESC.\n- **dw_2957** — Geometric mean per academic year over `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL JOIN ACADEMIC_TER