, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SIS_DEPARTMENT; incoming from LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE. Member of concept_subject_offering_facts and concept_course_material_programs; columns mapped to term_code, subject_id, department_name, enrollment_measures, master_subject_id concepts.\n- Graph traversal on **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER, SIS_DEPARTMENT, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; incoming from TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED, etc. Same concept/column-concept memberships.\n- Metric lineage: dw_1301 depends on LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED + ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (year grouping precedent); dw_2957/dw_4325 depend on ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL/ACADEMIC_TERMS; dw_4701 depends on library reserve tables + ACADEMIC_TERMS.\n- Hint-provided join keys confirm: `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE`.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix** (evidence: table `columns`/`desc` from semantic_get; concept comparisons):\n\n| Dimension | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | ACADEMIC_TERMS | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per term (all terms) | one row per term (status-tracked subset) | one row per subject per term, library scope | one row per subject per term, TIP scope |\n| Coverage | superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS (concept comparison \"Row coverage\") | subset | library reserve program subjects only (column_concept_enrollment_measures: \"may not cover all subjects\") | textbook program subjects only |\n| Unique fields | — | IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE, DROP_DATE | COURSE_NUMBER_DESC, parent of reserve detail | IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL, parent of TIP_DETAIL |\n| Year attributes | ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC (both present) | ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC (both present) | none (joins via TERM_CODE) | none (joins via TERM_CODE) |\n| Join risk | 1:1 on TERM_CODE with ACADEMIC_TERMS (both one row per term — no fan-out) | same | fact-to-dim many:1, no fan-out | fact-to-dim many:1, no fan-out |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n\n| Atomic requirement | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | ACADEMIC_TERMS | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| academic year + description output | SUPPORTED (ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC) | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED (no year cols) | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| geometric mean of enrolled students in *library* subjects, >0 filter | n/a | n/a | SUPPORTED (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; dw_1301 precedent) | VIOLATES semantics (TIP scope ≠ library) |\n| distinct departments offering *such* (library) subjects | n/a | n/a | SUPPORTED (OFFER_DEPT_CODE per hint mapping) | NOT-SUPPORTED for this requirement |\n| count of subjects offered per term (for range/var/stddev) | n/a | n/a | not the hinted source | SUPPORTED per hint (TERM_CODE grouping; one row per subject per term) |\n| \"terms where at least one subject was offered\" | n/a | n/a | n/a | SUPPORTED (HAVING COUNT ≥ 1 on per-term groups) |\n| join path to terms | SUPPORTED (TERM_CODE) | SUPPORTED (TERM_CODE) | via TERM_CODE | via TERM_CODE |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"academic year / academic year description\" → `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR` / `.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC` (hint mapping; column_concept_year_columns decision guide: yearly statistics over terms use term-table year columns).\n- \"library subjects … number of enrolled students\" → `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (column_concept_enrollment_measures decision guide: library-scope enrollment uses this column; excludes TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS and SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER).\n- \"more than zero enrolled students\" → `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0` (also guarantees LN() is defined for the geometric mean).\n- \"departments that offered such subjects\" → `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (hint mapping), counted DISTINCT.\n- \"number of subjects offered per academic term\" → per-TERM_CODE row count of `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (hint maps all of range/variance/stddev/variability to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE; table granularity is one row per subject per term, so COUNT(*) = subject count).\n- \"geometric mean\" → `EXP(AVG(LN(x)))` (dw_4701, dw_2957 precedents).\n- \"at least 20% greater/less than the average … across all years\" → dw_3131/dw_2580 precedent implements this as `> avg*1.2` / `< avg*0.8` with CROSS JOIN of the overall average.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- Library-enrollment-per-year statistics precedents: 1 — dw_1301 (STDDEV of LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS grouped by ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL year).\n- Geometric-mean-per-year precedents: 2 — dw_4701 (library reserve scope), dw_2957 (term tables).\n- ±20% HIGH/LOW/AVERAGE classification precedents: 2 — dw_3131, dw_2580 (both `> avg*1.2` / `< avg*0.8`).\n- Range/VARIANCE/STDDEV triple precedents: 2 — dw_4325, dw_3311 (both `MAX-MIN`, `VARIANCE()`, bare `STDDEV()`).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**: canonical source of ACADEMIC_YEAR/ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC in yearly rollups (dw_1301, dw_2957, dw_4325); joined on TERM_CODE by virtually every fact table.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: used when term status/regular-term filtering is needed and as the join partner of TIP facts (dw_2580, dw_4701); joined 1:1 to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL on TERM_CODE (dw_2957).\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: serves library-reserve enrollment questions (dw_1301, dw_3311, dw_1221, dw_3393); parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: serves textbook-program subject-count/enrollment questions (dw_1165, dw_3973, dw_4558); parent of TIP_DETAIL.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n| Entity | Tools called |\n|---|---|\n| ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | semantic_search, semantic_get, graph (via LIBRARY/TIP neighbor traversal) |\n| ACADEMIC_TERMS | semantic_search, semantic_get, graph neighbors |\n| LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph query_neighbors (both) |\n| TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | semantic_search, semantic_get, semantic_graph query_neighbors (both) |\n| dw_1301, dw_4701, dw_2957, dw_3131, dw_2580, dw_4325, dw_3311 | semantic_search, semantic_get (full SQL) |\n| concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_material_programs | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n| column_concept_year_columns, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_enrollment_measures | semantic_search, semantic_get |\n\nNote: `mysql_query` verification was attempted three times but the database rejected all connections (\"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\"), so data-level verification (join match rates, NULL enrollment counts) could not be executed. The SQL below is constructed strictly from documented granularity (one row per term in both term tables → no fan-out; one row per subject per term in both fact tables) and precedent SQL patterns.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:**\n- Year spine & labels: `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC` (hint mapping; dw_1301/dw_2957 precedent).\n- Library side: `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED` joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL on TERM_CODE; measure `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` with filter `> 0`; department count `COUNT(DISTINCT OFFER_DEPT_CODE)`; geometric mean `EXP(AVG(LN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)))`.\n- TIP side (two-level aggregation): inner per `TERM_CODE` (TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL) `COUNT(*)` with `HAVING COUNT(*) >= 1`; outer per year `MAX-MIN`, `VARIANCE()`, bare `STDDEV()`.\n- Classification: CROSS JOIN overall `AVG(subjects_stddev)`; `> avg*1.2` → HIGH_VARIABILITY, `< avg*0.8` → LOW_VARIABILITY, else AVERAGE (dw_3131 pattern).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** CTE `lib_stats` (year-grain library aggregates), CTE `term_counts` (term-grain TIP subject counts), CTE `tip_stats` (year-grain dispersion of term counts), CTE `combined` (inner join on year + year desc), final SELECT with CROSS JOIN average and CASE, ordered by geometric mean DESC. Caveats: `> 0` filter makes LN safe; term-table joins are 1:1 on TERM_CODE so no fan-out; bare STDDEV()/VARIANCE() per instructions.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: both term tables are one row per term (documented granularity) → TERM_CODE joins cannot fan out; fact tables are one row per subject per term → COUNT(*) equals subject count; NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS physically exists in LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (verified via columns definition).\n- **Semantic network**: concept_academic_term_dimension decision guide prescribes ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL for year attributes joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS when both are needed; column_concept_enrollment_measures prescribes LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS for library-scope enrollment; hint join keys match documented graph edges.\n- **Business**: dw_1301 is a same-shape precedent (yearly library enrollment statistics via ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL); dw_4701/dw_2957 establish EXP(AVG(LN())) geometric means per year ordered DESC; dw_3131/dw_2580 establish the ±20% classification implementation; dw_4325/dw_3311 establish the MAX−MIN / VARIANCE / STDDEV triple.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** ACADEMIC_TERMS alone could supply the year labels, but the hints and dw_1301 precedent anchor the year output to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (widest coverage); classification thresholds use strict `>`/`<` per both classification precedents (dw_3131, dw_2580) even though the wording says \"at least\" — the precedents are the tie-breaker. Database unavailability prevented empirical verification; the SQL follows documented 1:1/many:1 join cardinalities so results are deterministic given the schema.\n\n",
